Hi

Would'nt it be great to have body parts in nethack ?
Hits bn monsters would be much more interesting, think about
"the orc cut of your left arm"
"Kablamm, you stepped on a land mine... and lost your right leg"
"Oh no, he cut your head off,  ... you die"
Loosing one leg could slow you down, loosing both legs, you can only crawl,
loosing one arm, you can't use 2-handed weapons or a shield and you can't
wear 2 rings.
Loosing one eye ? Loosing both eyes and you're blind, permanently.
Loosing youre teeth, eating take 5 or more times as long and you can't eat
some of the tougher monsters (i.e. dragons).
Being kicked in the a** by a giant, you can't sit for 100 turns.
Loosing your head, .... well.

Hits that cause loss of body parts should be rare (one in 20 at best) and
dependend on armor class and relative level of monster and character.
A Giant should be more able to cut a first level Ac 7 thief into pieces
than an orc would be with a 5th level, Ac -1 fighter.
And hits on the head should be extremly hard to achieve (one in 1000 or so)

Of course, there should be some way to get missing body parts back,
a potion of regeneration would restore one random missing body part, a
blessed one would restore all and when you quaff a cursed one, you loose one
additional part. Cut off body parts should be items. You can take them to
special rooms, ambulances, filled with nurses and surgeons, who put them
back in place. But you should do it fast, or put it into an ice box.
Healers should be able to put themselves together alone, or there should be
a surgery equipment.
What about eating body parts ? Perhaps your own ?
Sacrifying body parts ? Polymorphing them ? Into what ?

What monsters can do to the players, players should be able to do to the
monsters. Cutting of Medusas head (and using it, but don't fall down the
stairs) of cutting of tentacles from an octopi ?

Some items should work only on some body parts. Like a cursed potion of
invisibility that makes only one body part invisible.

Seems that the game would be much more interesting, especially if this
ideas are combined with "nethack chemistry".

Enough suggestions ?

